      "dom_id": "question-8182",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the solutions of the equation $3{x}^{2}+25=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+25 & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & =-25 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-\\frac{25}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nx=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{25}{3}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $x$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{25}{3}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{3}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{25}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rationalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\pm \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
